From 9c12403efb1b3fd2fb71125827b92fae5eebaabb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:21:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] airpods: add BluetoothDevice#setAirPodsMusicDuck behind
 MANAGE_AIRPODS_IDENTITY

The audio hardening of this OS ignores an app's own AudioManager volume calls,
so the AirPods app cannot lower the music while the owner speaks (conversation
awareness). Add a narrow call instead, run in the Bluetooth process, which the
hardening exempts by uid: only for a bonded device registered through
setAirPodsIdentity that is the active A2DP device, percent one of 20, 35, 50
or 70, never raising the volume or going below the stream minimum, restoring
only if the volume is still the value it set. The volume is given back when the
caller dies, when the AirPods are routed away and on unbond or adapter off. The
death watch is generalised so the route and the duck share it.

airpods: rename the nested duck record that clashes with java.lang.Record

Error Prone rejects a nested class named Record (JavaLangClash), which stopped
the Bluetooth module build. Rename it to Ducked.

airpods: accept a music duck percent from 10 to 90

The owner chose a continuous slider for how loud the music stays while they speak (Plan 7B), so setAirPodsMusicDuck takes any integer from 10 to 90 instead of 20, 35, 50 or 70. Every other limit stays: STREAM_MUSIC only, only while the registered device is the active A2DP device, only lowering, never below the stream minimum, restore only if the volume is still the value this call set, restore on caller death, disconnect, unbond and adapter off.
